# Visualforce Basics (Overview)

## Introduction

Visualforce is a framework used to build custom Salesforce pages and user interfaces.

---

## Features

- Tag-based markup language
- Apex controller integration
- Custom page development
- Server-side rendering

---

## Basic Visualforce Page

```html
<apex:page>
    <h1>Hello Salesforce</h1>
</apex:page>
```

---

## Visualforce with Controller

### Apex Controller

```apex
public class HelloController {

    public String message {
        get {
            return 'Hello Salesforce';
        }
    }
}
```

### Visualforce Page

```html
<apex:page controller="HelloController">

    {!message}

</apex:page>
```

---

## Common Components

```html
<apex:inputText />
```

```html
<apex:commandButton value="Save" />
```

```html
<apex:pageBlock title="Account Details">
</apex:pageBlock>
```

---

## Advantages

- Easy customization
- Apex integration
- Flexible layouts
- Salesforce security support

---

## Conclusion

Visualforce remains useful for legacy applications and specialized custom pages.
